{
  "comment": [
    "Single source of truth for the built-in insert-effect registry. One row per",
    "released built-in effect, in effect-type order (the row order IS the ABI",
    "effect-type order; effectValue must equal the public VN_EFFECT_* value).",
    "gen_effect_registry.py turns this into the checked-in compile-time registry",
    "header consumed by the render dispatch and the effect pool. Adding a built-in",
    "effect is one row here plus its kernels/hooks in BuiltinEffects.cpp; the",
    "generated static_asserts fail the build if a row disagrees with the public",
    "enum value, parameter-count constant, or state type.",
    "",
    "Each row's params array is the metadata authority for that effect's private",
    "parameter index space: one entry per index, in index order (entry i describes",
    "parameter index i). It declares every parameter's unit, combination domain,",
    "neutral (identity) contribution, resolved-value clamp, and transition support,",
    "so a bound parameter's contributions compose by a declared rule instead of",
    "implicit last-writer-wins. combine domains: AddDb (contributions sum in dB on",
    "the base), Multiply (commutative product on the base, neutral 1), AddLogHz /",
    "AddLogQ / AddLogTime (base * 2^sum, a log-2 octave shift), None (binding unsupported;",
    "attaching a binding to it is refused). Every clamp equals the released",
    "validator's accepted range EXACTLY -- never tighter, never looser -- so a",
    "composed value reaching the audio thread always passes ValidateEffectParam",
    "and never suppresses a valid update. The validator's open lower bound (delay,",
    "freq, and Q accept value > 0) is expressed as clampMin \"strictlyPositive\",",
    "which resolves to the smallest positive float. Open upper bounds use clampMax",
    "\"strictlyBelowOne\" for value < 1 and \"nyquist\" for value strictly below",
    "0.5 * sampleRate; Q upper stays 100. A generated static_assert pins each row's",
    "params length to its parameter-count constant."
  ],
